ublic/email%20template/images/1787204910703-b0a6d3b9-f48a-4f60-b747-15d84d5c54fc.png" style="display:block;maxWidth:100%;height:333px;margin:0 auto 16px;border:0;width:584px;"/><p style="font-family:Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;font-size:15px;line-height:1.6;color:#374151;margin:0 0 12px;text-align:left;"></p><p style="color:rgb(34, 34, 34);font-size:small;background-color:rgb(255, 255, 255);"><span style="color:rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.9);"><span style="font-size:14px;"><span style="font-family:&quot;Gilda Display&quot;, serif;">               For a long time, hardware companies competed by building better products-Better specifications, Better performance, More features, Lower cost.<br/><br/>That model worked when technology advantages lasted for years. Today, they often last for months!<br/><br/>A feature introduced by one company quickly becomes standard across the category. Global supply chains have matured, manufacturing access has expanded, and competitors can replicate technical improvements faster than ever before.<br/><br/>According to McKinsey, product life cycles across industries have reduced by nearly 4x over the past 50 years.<br/><br/>This is fundamentally changing differentiation in hardware. Because when technical advantages become easier to replicate, products slowly begin competing on familiarity instead of originality. And eventually, categories start looking interchangeable.<br/><br/>We see this across appliances, consumer electronics, wearables, IoT products and lifestyle hardware. Specifications improve every year. But the emotional distance between products keeps shrinking.<br/><br/>This is where commoditization begins. Not because products are poorly engineered. But because customers stop experiencing meaningful distinction between one product and another.<br/><br/>Research in consumer behavior consistently shows that customers form first impressions within seconds, heavily influencing perceived quality, trust and purchase intent long before specifications are evaluated.<br/><br/>That means customers are evaluating far more than features-<br/>How refined the proportions feel.<br/>How precise the fit and finish looks.<br/>How confidently materials are handled.<br/>How recognizable the design language becomes.<br/>How consistent the product feels across a portfolio.<br/><br/>This is one of the reasons brands like Apple, Dyson, Braun and Nothing continue creating preference even in crowded markets. Their advantage is not only technology. It is recognition.<br/><br/>At </span></span></span><a href="https://www.linkedin.com/company/iuovadesigncompany/" target="_blank" data-saferedirecturl="https://www.google.com/url?q=https://www.linkedin.com/company/iuovadesigncompany/&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1787288643021000&amp;usg=AOvVaw1FYus6mI6N2KWrSk63UZW4" style="color:rgb(10, 102, 194);box-sizing:inherit;margin:0px;padding:0px;font-size:14px;vertical-align:baseline;background-image:none;background-position:0% 0%;background-size:auto;background-repeat:repeat;background-attachment:scroll;background-origin:padding-box;background-clip:border-box;font-weight:600;border-color:rgb(10, 102, 194);border-style:none;border-width:0px;font-family:-apple-system, system-ui, BlinkMacSystemFont, &quot;Segoe UI&quot;, Roboto, &quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;, &quot;Fira Sans&quot;, Ubuntu, Oxygen, &quot;Oxygen Sans&quot;, Cantarell, &quot;Droid Sans&quot;, &quot;Apple Color Emoji&quot;, &quot;Segoe UI Emoji&quot;, &quot;Segoe UI Emoji&quot;, &quot;Segoe UI Symbol&quot;, &quot;Lucida Grande&quot;, Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif;word-break:normal;line-height:inherit !important;"><strong><span style="font-family:&quot;Gilda Display&quot;, serif;">Iuova Design Company</span></strong></a><span style="color:rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.9);"><span style="font-size:14px;"><span style="font-family:&quot;Gilda Display&quot;, serif;">, one question we often discuss during product development is-<br/>“Will this product still feel distinctive after the next five competitors enter the category?”<br/><br/>Because long-term brand value is rarely built through specifications alone.<br/>It is built through memorability, consistency and emotional familiarity over time!</span><span style="font-family:-apple-system, system-ui, BlinkMacSystemFont, &quot;Segoe UI&quot;, Roboto, &quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;, &quot;Fira Sans&quot;, Ubuntu, Oxygen, &quot;Oxygen Sans&quot;, Cantarell, &quot;Droid Sans&quot;, &quot;Apple Color Emoji&quot;, &quot;Segoe UI Emoji&quot;, &quot;Segoe UI Emoji&quot;, &quot;Segoe UI Symbol&quot;, &quot;Lucida Grande&quot;, Helv;"><br/><br/></span></span></span></p><div id="ikhagf" draggable="true" style="height:32px;line-height:32px;font-size:0;"> </div><strong id="iy6cog" draggable="true"><span id="ipyok4" draggable="true" style="font-family:&quot;Gilda Display&quot;, serif;">You may explore our capabilities and selected projects in our company catalogue.</span></strong><p></p><ul style="color:rgb(34, 34, 34);font-size:small;margin-bottom:0px;background-color:rgb(255, 255, 255);"><li style="margin-left:15px;"><p style="margin:0px;padding:0px;word-break:break-word;line-height:1.5;letter-spacing:0px;direction:ltr;"><strong><span style="color:rgb(65, 55, 54);"><span style="font-size:14px;"><span style="font-family:&quot;Gilda Display&quot;, serif;">Instagram</span></span></span></strong><span style="color:rgb(65, 55, 54);"><span style="font-size:14px;"><span style="font-family:&quot;Gilda Display&quot;, serif;"> -</span></span></span><span style="color:rgb(0, 97, 254);"><span style="font-size:14px;"><span style="font-family:&quot;Gilda Display&quot;, serif;"> </span></span></span><a href="https://www.instagram.com/iuovadesign/" target="_blank" data-saferedirecturl="https://www.google.com/url?q=https://www.instagram.com/iuovadesign/&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1787288643021000&amp;usg=AOvVaw1Bq0cyll4RyJZdr4yjxV7i" style="color:rgb(5, 90, 228);word-break:break-word;direction:ltr;"><strong><span style="font-size:14px;"><span style=