er;"><p>Dear {{first_name}},</p><p>What if {{company}} could access a dedicated design and engineering team without the cost, complexity, and overhead of building one internally? Our Innovation Retainer is designed to give growing businesses consistent access to experienced specialists who can support everything from product ideation and concept development to detailed engineering, DFM-ready CAD, FEA analysis, embedded design, prototyping, and packaging. Instead of managing multiple vendors or hiring a large in-house team, you get one structured engagement with a dedicated team focused on understanding your products, priorities, and business goals. Each month, the engagement can include multiple concept sprints, ongoing design and engineering support, strategic reviews, technical documentation, and structured IP and handoff processes, allowing your team to move ideas from early concepts toward production with greater speed and confidence. The model is flexible enough to support both short-term development needs and long-term innovation programs, while giving you predictable access to the expertise required at each stage of the product development cycle. I’d love to understand what {{company}} is currently working on and explore whether this approach could help your team accelerate upcoming projects without adding unnecessary overhead. If this sounds relevant, I’d be happy to walk you through how the engagement works and put together a tailored proposal based on your specific requirements.</p><p>Warm regards,</p><p>Rupali Sirsath | IUOVA</p></p></body></html>	gbf	Hi {{first_name}},\n\nProduct innovation at {{company}} doesn't have to take months. Our <strong>Discovery Sprint</strong> — a focused 3-day engagement — surfaces hidden product opportunities, maps engineering risk, and produces a decision-ready innovation brief.\n\n<strong>What you get:</strong>\n\n• Market gap analysis & competitor audit\n• 3 concept directions with DFM feasibility\n• Engineering risk matr